{
  "items": [
    {"n": 1, "name": "First screen", "score": 1, "reason": "The headline, decision block and c1 make the call clear: keep September. qwen3.8-flash is worse on character (-7.6 pts, -12.9 to -1.8), and both candidates cost more. The lede and Watch name the main risk, an unnamed provider routing. But the headline puts '27–28% more to run' down to the models themselves, when the cost belongs to this run's routing. An earlier high-confidence round found the opposite for qwen3.8-flash. A reader who stops at the headline gets the cost order as a fact about the models."},
    {"n": 2, "name": "Coherent story", "score": 1, "reason": "No block contradicts its claim: c1's rows match its sentences, and c2's intervals are clear of zero. Two things slow a reader. The decision says qwen3.8-flash costs '$0.62 per 1,000 replies more', but the options table right beside it shows $2.43 against $1.89, a $0.54 gap. The $0.62 is a paired figure over 284 cases, and the page never says so. Also, c4 opens with 'off-lane failures look alike across arms', then says the qwen3.8-flash card fails a different way: it answers the request outright. The judge's reasons on all three qwen3.8-flash off-lane cards back that difference."},
    {"n": 3, "name": "Honest emphasis", "score": 1, "reason": "The candidates' weak axes are visible, and 1017's pass rate is correctly 'not told apart' (-7.4 to +2.6). But the confidence line reads High and calls the cost gap 'measured telemetry' that settles the call alone. Yet the page's own Next calls repricing on a named routing 'the one result that could reverse the call'. An earlier round, held at high confidence, found qwen3.8-flash lowers production cost. That overstates how settled the deciding axis is."},
    {"n": 4, "name": "Sound elision", "score": 2, "reason": "Nothing omitted would change the decision. The judged outcome and transcript scores, the booth-stays-offstage score and the delivery check go the same way or are not separated. The confirmatory readings don't move with the margin: the margin sweep holds at every value, with 1017 flipping at 5.8 and qwen3.8-flash at 10.8 without changing the call. Measuring spend is rightly kept apart from production cost."},
    {"n": 5, "name": "Confounds handled", "score": 1, "reason": "c1 and c2 carry the reasoning-share confound on 1017, and Next steps proposes a rerun at matched reasoning. c3 reads 1017's holds-character loss (-4.7, -8.7 to -0.6), which carries that confound, but c3 states no caveat. The model-confound clause in the confidence line says what would make it matter but not why the call holds until then."},
    {"n": 6, "name": "Actionable next steps", "score": 2, "reason": "Each step names an experiment and what it would settle: repricing on a named routing (could reopen the call), an off-lane directive rerun, 1017 at September's reasoning share, and judge calibration against human ratings."},
    {"n": 7, "name": "Evidence fits claims", "score": 1, "reason": "c1's and c2's forests show their claims' own figures. c3's headline figures are not in its block: the loss shares (48% and 53%) and September's 65.8% off-lane rate. The block draws only per-stratum changes. Its caption mentions 'bold rows' that the table doesn't mark. c2's block carries two captions."}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {"claim": "report", "severity": "must_fix", "finding": "The call rests on cost alone: the confidence line says 'the cost gap, which alone rules out both candidates'. Yet the headline, the Recommendation ('it costs the least to run') and c2's text put the cost order down to the models with no provider named. The run does not record who served each arm, and an earlier high-confidence round found qwen3.8-flash lowers production cost. The confidence still reads High and calls the cost gap 'measured telemetry', with no clause on routing. Fix: (1) scope the headline, Recommendation and c2 sentences to 'on this run's unnamed provider routing'. (2) Add a confidence clause saying the High covers the cost order on this routing only, that a named routing pricing a candidate at or below $1.89 per 1,000 replies would reopen the call, and why it holds until then (the prior result was on an unknown routing too). Otherwise lower the confidence. (3) Give the model-confound clause a reason the call holds until then, as the other clauses do.", "continues": "new"},
    {"claim": "c2", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "The decision and c2 cite +$0.62 and +$0.49 per 1,000 replies, but the options table shows $2.43 and $2.41 against $1.89, gaps of about $0.54 and $0.52. The cited figures are paired changes over the cases where both arms reported cost (284 and 293 cases), and the 27–28% comes from the arm means. Say this in c2 and the decision, or quote the table's gaps there, so a reader doesn't take the figures for an error. Also note that 1017's 'would more likely widen' rests on inference, since output tokens were not reported. Drop the duplicate caption on c2's block.", "continues": "new"},
    {"claim": "c3", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "c3 reads 1017's holds-character loss, which carries the reasoning-share confound, but states no caveat. Attach it as c1 does. Also put the claim's own figures in its block: the off-lane loss shares (48% for qwen3.8-flash, 53% for 1017) and September's off-lane rate of 65.8%. Remove or honour the caption's reference to bold rows, since none are marked. 'The weak spot for every model' holds among the eight strata shown, but the 'assistant shape' stratum (6 cases) is lower for September (58.8%). Say 'among the larger strata'.", "continues": "new"},
    {"claim": "c4", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "c4 opens with 'off-lane failures look alike across arms, September included', then says qwen3.8-flash fails differently: it answers the out-of-lane ask outright. Its sampled cards (landlord email, jeans wash, phone choice) all do. Lead with the difference instead: 1017 and September slip into narration or help-desk phrasing, while qwen3.8-flash gives the off-lane help. Say the pattern rests on 3 cards kept from 64 qwen3.8-flash failures.", "continues": "new"}
  ],
  "resolved": []
}
