    {"claim": "c2", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "c2 says September has 'its own missing trials at its p95 cost ($2.02 per 1,000 replies)'. Read that way, $2.02 is September's p95, but its p95 is $5.30 per 1,000 replies. $2.02 is September's mean once its 33 trials with no reported cost are filled in at $5.30 each. The conclusion holds, since $2.24 and $2.36 are both above $2.02. Reword it, for example: 'September's mean, with its 33 missing trials set to its p95 cost of $5.30, would be $2.02 per 1,000 replies.'", "continues": "new"},
    {"claim": "c3", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "The left-out note on small strata says only September's 'assistant shape' rate (58.8%) is below its off-lane rate. 1017's is too: 44.4% in assistant shape against 45.6% off-lane. Name both arms in that note. Also, 'the eight largest strata' includes lineage, which has 10 cases, but pushback, rejection, short and story have 10 cases as well. Either say 'strata of 10 or more cases' or say how the tie was broken. Off-lane is still the lowest for every arm among all of them.", "continues": "new"}
  ],
